# Compiled command entry points built into the workspace bin folder
/bin/

# No fixture binary rule is needed. The only remaining fixture is the TopsailAI
# Provider's conformance stand-in, which lives inside that provider workspace and
# is always built with an explicit -o under .tmp/, so it never drops a binary
# beside its source. The two root-anchored rules that used to sit here named
# fixtures that no longer exist.

# Provider workspaces need no binary rule of their own. Each provider Makefile
# passes an explicit -o under its own .tmp/bin, and .tmp/ is ignored at any
# depth. A bare `go build ./src` inside a provider workspace cannot drop a stray
# binary either: go names the output after the package directory, which is the
# src directory itself, so the build refuses rather than writing beside it.
